Well it's possible as long as you are aware that the ref to the method will change and that you have to bind the reference to the search method yourself.

A very naive example of delay:

```js
searchFunction: function(helper) {
  const search = helper.search.bind(helper);
  setTimeout(function(){
    search();
  }, 10);
}
```

This would work. What about we provide the search method as a standalone function along the helper? (this is one of the point I want to discuss Thursday)
